            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.38678/2610.38678v1/figure/kvem_annotation_interface.png",
                "caption": "Figure 8:Web interface for KVEM annotation.Annotators review each event together with its tracked entities and keyframes, refine entity bounding boxes when necessary, select the gold entity, and annotate the temporal decision windows for streaming interaction. The interface also supports event-level query annotation and visualization of the corresponding timeline, facilitating consistent construction of KVEM instances.",
                "position": 3061
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.38678/2610.38678v1/figure/kvem_verification_interface.png",
                "caption": "Figure 9:Web interface for KVEM human verification.The fully masked video and the revealed video, in which only the gold entity is visible, are presented side by side for comparison. Annotators jointly inspect the query, gold entity, and ASK candidates to verify that the masked video contains no information leakage, that revealing the requested gold entity is sufficient to uniquely answer the query, and that the correct and incorrect ASK options correspond to appropriate and inappropriate information requests, respectively.",
                "position": 3067
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.38678/2610.38678v1/figure/vim_annotation_interface.png",
                "caption": "Figure 10:Multi-view annotation interface for the VIM task.The interface presents temporally synchronized egocentric and multiple exocentric video streams from Ego-Exo4D, together with the key-step-based turn structure and temporal decision windows. Annotators jointly inspect all viewpoints, designate the initial viewpoint, identify alternative viewpoints that reveal the missing visual evidence, and construct viewpoint-dependent queries and ASK candidates.",
                "position": 3073
            },
